I'm Melany, a first-gen Mexican American born and raised in Northwest Arkansas. I'm the third of four kids and the only daughter, which means I grew up learning to hold my own and to laugh a lot. These days, my brothers and I have all found our way back under one roof, and we share a house. Everyone pitches in, and somehow it works.

I'm the first in my family to attend college, and I'm working toward being the first to graduate. That's something I carry with gratitude, and with the hope that it helps pave the way for the generations after me. I recently transferred from NWACC to the University of Arkansas as a sophomore, and I'm thankful to be part of the College of Engineering and to learn from the people and opportunities here.

My mind is always busy, and I do my best when I'm active. During the semester, you'll find me lifting, cooking, practicing yoga, studying, serving my community, or at church events. When I'm off the clock, I'm with family and friends, outside, or dancing.
